From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 07:32:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 115/117] senemos: document Linux 7.3-rc2 source identity

---
 senemos/README.md | 20 ++++++++++++++------
 senemos/build.sh  |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/senemos/README.md b/senemos/README.md
index 2cd7b0125533..d0b8a8b0132c 100644
--- a/senemos/README.md
+++ b/senemos/README.md
@@ -1,9 +1,11 @@
-# Senemos Nabu Linux 7.2 port
+# Senemos Nabu Linux 7.3 mainline port
 
-The `7.2.0` branch rebases Xiaomi Pad 5 (`nabu`) support onto the verified
-Linux 7.2 release tarball. The upstream archive SHA-256 is:
+This branch rebases Xiaomi Pad 5 (`nabu`) support onto the official Linux
+`v7.3-rc2` tag (peeled commit
+`df2908090cda368b01ff43709f51890076c56157`). The kernel.org release archive
+`linux-7.3-rc2.tar.gz` has SHA-256:
 
-`f9fef3d14c0df53819026f4be74459835c2a0b0dcbf5b5bbd9ea19f0829402b3`
+`6b97fb9397172e95ed95b56a78524a184bf186858bea7a271b9ebe81a0e57417`
 
 The comparison baseline is the consolidated `6.17.0` source branch at commit
 `d5731dcf7d5e418483d62f65b03266206b133f88`, whose Linux 6.17 archive
@@ -19,6 +21,12 @@ double-tap wake, PM8150B charger and fuel gauge, legacy ADSP/APR audio,
 FastRPC mount matrices, tablet-mode reporting, late optional XHCI policy and
 IDT P9418 stylus charging support.
 
+The media port preserves Linux 7.3's current Iris architecture while adapting
+the Nabu VPU5 firmware protocol, queue layout, buffer requirements, VP9/P010
+formats, dual-core load assignment and suspend lifecycle. Camera support also
+exposes the board calibration EEPROMs and keeps each sensor independently
+enumerable.
+
 The final 6.17 delta is also carried: pogo-keyboard power/detect and dynamic
 tablet-mode reporting, Xiaomi HID pointer filtering, WCN3990 single-channel
 scan handling, post-enable DSI/touch wake ordering, and the P9418 event and
@@ -41,11 +49,11 @@ The script recreates the output configuration from the Fedora Rawhide arm64
 base plus `nabu-minimal.config`, and builds `Image`, the Nabu DTB and all
 modules. The resulting ABI is:
 
-`7.2.x-nabu-senemos-mainline-unstable`
+`7.3-rc2-nabu-senemos-mainline-unstable`
 
 The default output directory is:
 
-`/workspace/kernel-builds/linux-nabu-senemos-v7.2.0-linux-7.2`
+`/workspace/kernel-builds/linux-nabu-senemos-mainline-unstable`
 
 Source review, successful compilation, DT schema validation and RPM/COPR
 publication are separate gates. None of them proves boot, display, touch,
diff --git a/senemos/build.sh b/senemos/build.sh
index acc878f4d597..f17764bf37a8 100755
--- a/senemos/build.sh
+++ b/senemos/build.sh
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ output_dir=${SENEMOS_OUTPUT_DIR:-/workspace/kernel-builds/linux-nabu-senemos-mai
 jobs=${SENEMOS_JOBS:-16}
 
 # Keep the release deterministic. An explicitly set empty LOCALVERSION stops
-# setlocalversion from appending "+" merely because HEAD is past upstream-v7.2.
+# setlocalversion from appending "+" merely because HEAD is past v7.3-rc2.
 export LOCALVERSION=${SENEMOS_EXTRA_LOCALVERSION:-}
 
 mkdir -p "$output_dir"
